details.image_prompt:
[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features two simple, matte ceramic bowls set on an aged, warm oak kitchen table. The composition is a 3/4 overhead angle, ensuring every component is clearly identifiable within the frame while maintaining generous negative space around the edges. Shallow depth of field keeps the primary bowl in sharp focus, while the second bowl and a blurred glass of water sit in the background. Lighting is soft, natural side light from a window to the left, casting gentle shadows and highlighting the glistening textures of the dish. Props include a casual, rumpled linen napkin tucked under the foreground bowl and a small, weathered wooden spoon resting on the table, alongside a few scattered cherry tomato halves and a fresh lemon half with visible zest texture. The dish consists of a hearty mix of browned, savory ground turkey, tender quinoa, vibrant diced zucchini, and burst cherry tomatoes, all tossed with wilted bright-green spinach leaves. The colors are a rustic blend of golden-brown turkey, pale translucent quinoa, deep forest green spinach, and bright ruby-red tomato skins. The texture is homey and moist, with subtle oil sheen and visible flecks of dried oregano. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating—lived-in, warm, authentic. Not a sterile studio setup. Include subtle traces of the cooking process: a small, scattered herb leaf and a tiny juice stain on the table. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. The image should be indistinguishable from a photograph taken by a professional food photographer for a printed cookbook."
]
